WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.220
A mushroom stays in one place, like a plant.

2
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.340
So why don't scientists call it a plant?

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.240
The answer depends on your tools.

4
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:19.053
Here are six living things: a mushroom, an oak, a deer, a paramecium, a bacterium

5
00:00:19.073 --> 00:00:24.313
and an archaeon. Scientists sort living things with several kinds of evidence.

6
00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:28.253
This ladder orders them; it is not a timeline.

7
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.117
The bottom rung is your eyes.

8
00:00:32.297 --> 00:00:35.677
The mushroom stays put, like the oak, so it sits with the plants.

9
00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:41.157
The deer has an animal's body and walks away, so it goes with the animals.

10
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.817
The three tiny ones are too small to make out.

11
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:49.557
For a long time, many scientists grouped mushrooms with plants.

12
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.620
Next rung, the light microscope.

13
00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.280
It answers three questions.

14
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.760
Does each cell have a nucleus, the part that holds its DNA?

15
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.600
Which cell parts does it have?

16
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.120
Does it have one cell or many?

17
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.300
A fourth question needs other tests.

18
00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.740
Does it make its own food, or take food in?

19
00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:14.793
The first question splits the cards.

20
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:18.013
Four of them have cells with a nucleus.

21
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:23.833
The bacterium and the archaeon have no nucleus, and under the microscope they look

22
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:24.833
alike.

23
00:01:25.233 --> 00:01:26.973
Now zoom in on the mushroom.

24
00:01:28.313 --> 00:01:31.573
Its cells have a nucleus and a cell wall, like a plant's.

25
00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:37.033
But they have no chloroplasts, the green parts where a cell makes sugar using light.

26
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.463
So a mushroom cannot make its own food.

27
00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:44.603
It releases digesting substances into the log.

28
00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:50.363
They break the wood into tiny dissolved pieces, and the mushroom takes them in.

29
00:01:51.563 --> 00:01:53.583
Most plants make their own food instead.

30
00:01:54.763 --> 00:01:57.083
So the mushroom slides out of the plant group.

31
00:01:58.363 --> 00:02:00.463
Later, fungi got a kingdom of their own.

32
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:03.347
Third rung, cell chemistry.

33
00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:08.167
The bacterium and the archaeon look the same under a microscope.

34
00:02:09.547 --> 00:02:11.247
Are they the same kind of living thing?

35
00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:23.353
No. The chemicals that build their cell walls and membranes are different.

36
00:02:24.613 --> 00:02:27.353
Their genes, compared on the top rung, differ too.

37
00:02:28.613 --> 00:02:32.553
So scientists split them into two domains, Bacteria and Archaea.

38
00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:38.473
Every living thing whose cells have a nucleus goes in a third domain, Eukarya.

39
00:02:39.873 --> 00:02:41.213
So life has three domains.

40
00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:44.093
Kingdoms sit inside them.

41
00:02:45.413 --> 00:02:48.593
Fungi, plants and animals are kingdoms inside Eukarya.

42
00:02:49.853 --> 00:02:51.013
The paramecium waits.

43
00:02:52.253 --> 00:02:53.453
You will place it yourself.

44
00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:58.453
Look back. The living things never changed.

45
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:03.413
The evidence did, and new evidence could move a card to a new group.

46
00:03:04.433 --> 00:03:06.273
One rung is left, DNA.

47
00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.913
Scientists compare the same gene in different living things.

48
00:03:12.193 --> 00:03:15.373
Will the mushroom's gene match the oak's or the deer's more closely?
